### 1. File-based skill (widget-catalog) - must trigger load_skill then read_skill_resource,
### and the answer must contain the invented SKU / compatibility facts.
POST http://localhost:5060/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "prompt": "What is the SKU for the Aurora-9 Connector, and what is it compatible with per the compatibility notes?"
}

### 2. Inline skill (joke-teller)
POST http://localhost:5060/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "prompt": "Tell me a joke."
}

### 3. Class-based skill + script + approval gate (greeting-formalizer)
POST http://localhost:5060/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "prompt": "Formalize this greeting: hey there!!"
}

### 4. PR #67 (issue #66) proof: AgentRunOptions.AdditionalProperties["sessionId"] must reach the
### context-provider pipeline. Check the response's "sessionMemoryProof" object - all three fields
### must equal "demo-session-1". Before the fix, all three would be null.
POST http://localhost:5060/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "prompt": "Tell me a joke.",
    "sessionId": "demo-session-1"
}

### 5. Same as #4 but with no sessionId supplied - "sessionMemoryProof" should show all three fields
### as null, confirming the endpoint only sets AgentRunOptions when a session id is actually given.
POST http://localhost:5060/run
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "prompt": "Tell me a joke."
}
